        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq3MIoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz60QACn8PUQa+zSrJyYWTcj8Pabh\nu9ABAhlMqazmRWVtMu3GzP0ID9peZEblN0OnPmwwagYdrKUiWaYLhciFc0wc18lB\njw+NXUIJLDovlORJbfX6IEZ66LkNixFLgNZoLwsEdz/2ngfeHU/GevUgG1gzCyCs\ncpiS27L/DFkvbZTxDn2Er1TdBCh40CGBx+uxA0BFz9NLZKDMyB/tQTPXus70+4WU\nGDCYTxbHUajvycS6GWeLRT61WdWRKFY/JtHIFiuFpzg+AE/g6TdtKeBAf+jxHlM/\nxk5ZO87I8KDakwpkendWEmhJFAJZTrVt0gZEZKwcFhzrqRpCiEokkJNhlEmvN761\nKM9yemjKpqzWBTvyC+eHRoqz8zY0pnH2sZrOCSBnOpuyPxkYcqtRexF8fMf9X72N\nfIQGkPRE10cfx7SArLK3QZ7u6rGBpsMgzvV9Z1OjPOWA/qTx9/W/RubKV/N74cJP\nOHtCT3I3siQ9EBZYxarHdwasq8Mi+CxvW7D/ksjkYELVAwoMLda/5mhHbUSta15b\nlXKGkffsqoRbneoorjP6GPfYdWD0atVdWLrOcEKwSkGRDhvjua0x4VItb3mHLUmA\nADCfMvEwBYxfzrlpEOpwthy8whcdCP63IwqAMhYK/vBp9u36hoi38kOHxm4Vgl/y\ngVBqBU/hA/iYlgUZpLAd\n=Jjn9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 9e101df4f2c532a3db2c6d871e59b8f638c37edb\nparent de088fcec661a215df76e234c5375c952e2f5c58\nauthor Matt Van Horn <mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com> 1792852520 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792852520 +0800\n\nfeat(elf): inspect Linux kernel module metadata (#7010)\n\n* feat(elf): inspect Linux kernel module metadata\n\nAdds inspect-kernel-module and inspect_kernel_module for ELF32/ELF64\nET_REL Linux kernel modules, read statically without executing them.\nReports ordered .modinfo entries with duplicates preserved, __versions\nsymbol CRCs, the presence of .gnu.linkonce.this_module and __ksymtab,\n.init.text and .exit.text sizes, and an appended module signature\ntrailer with its PKCS#7 byte range and SHA-256. gzip, xz and zstd\ncontainers are reported unsupported with external decompression as the\nnext probe. Malformed headers and exhausted entry budgets return no\npartial success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016y53PdpyMAp9RSW65fatHe\n\n* fix(elf): bound kernel module ksymtab listing and tighten contracts\n\nCharge listed __ksymtab* sections against max_entries, omit section names\nlonger than 256 bytes with ksymtab_name_exceeds_limit, and aggregate the\nnon-file-backed limitation so repeated huge names cannot inflate Evidence.\nUse fixedTupleSchema for the signature pad bytes with projection parity\ntests, and assert the late-cancellation reason and retained observation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016y53PdpyMAp9RSW65fatHe\n\n* fix: resolve merge integration errors\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Van Horn <455140+mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
