  {
    "sha": "781760a195c9d90c1bd3d57ad9ff55e5461bfcd4",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOSB6hVdoAKDc4MTc2MGExOTVjOWQ5MGMxYmQzZDU3YWQ5ZmY1NWU1NDYxYmZjZDQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Matt Van Horn",
        "email": "mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-24T08:02:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-24T08:02:59Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(apple): inspect IPS crash reports (#6511)\n\n* feat(apple): inspect IPS crash reports\n\nAdd inspect_apple_ips for caller-selected Apple .ips files. Parse the\nfirst-line metadata object and, when bug_type is the string 309, the\ncrash body: process identity, exception and termination facts, threads,\nusedImages, lossless integer registers, and documented classification\nrules. Other bug types including 288 stackshots return no crash result.\nOpened Mach-O and dSYM UUID joins remain unobserved.\n\nRelated to #4297\n\n* fix(apple): keep IPS register literals exact\n\nUse the arm64e fixture integer that matches 0x8527000193ed4944 instead\nof an IEEE-754-rounded decimal, and count the lossless JSON example\nlength from the source text.\n\n* fix(apple): budget IPS parsing and keep typed presence\n\nParse the IPS metadata and crash body through a projection of the\ndocumented members. Members the report does not interpret are\nsyntax-checked without being materialized, and thread, frame, image and\nthe new max_registers budgets run before each row is parsed, so a large\nselected file fails with a typed resource error instead of first\nexpanding every row. Fixed allowances bound JSON nesting, unlisted key\nnames and termination reasons.\n\nPresent values whose JSON type differs from the documented one are no\nlonger read as absence: they are listed in coverage.type_mismatches and\ncoverage becomes partial, including wrong-type or missing threads and\nusedImages collections. osVersion keeps the producer dictionary or the\nstring form. Frame roles follow physical frame depth, so the top frame\nof a non-faulting thread is current_instruction and inlined rows share\nthe following frame's role. SIGKILL classes compare the canonical hex\nonce, so 0xdeadd0cc no longer matches dead10cc. Invalid UTF-8 is refused\ninstead of being replaced, and JSON strings are decoded by copying\nunescaped spans.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(apple): bound integer text expansion and reconcile coverage\n\n* refactor(apple): retain image metadata at its owning row\n\n* refactor(apple): validate row capacity through reconciled coverage\n\n* test(apple): verify resource recovery at the public error boundary\n\n* docs(apple): record complete IPS task and corpus measurements\n\n* docs(apple): record integrated checks and stdio corpus evidence\n\n* docs(apple): record PE integration and baseline cleanup controls\n\n* fix(native): bound IPS string decoding and preserve invalid identities\n\n* refactor(native): use exact optional IPS source evidence\n\n* docs(native): verify IPS escape capacity and complete-task costs\n\n* test(native): verify IPS through production stdio MCP\n\n* style(tests): format IPS advertised schema bindings\n\n* fix(native): preserve unresolved IPS references and recorded frame semantics\n\n* docs(native): record IPS reference review evidence\n\n* fix(apple-ips): enforce JSON and report consistency\n\n* docs(apple-ips): record final consistency verification\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Van Horn <455140+mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: gensokyo-dev <342580529+gensokyo-dev@users.noreply.github.com>",
