  {
    "sha": "4ef916da03d93729041f79cec0ee243cd2d3097d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOSB6hVdoAKDRlZjkxNmRhMDNkOTM3MjkwNDFmNzljZWMwZWUyNDNjZDJkMzA5N2Q",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Matt Van Horn",
        "email": "mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-24T03:44:12Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-24T03:44:12Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(pe): inspect import and delay-load tables (#6509)\n\n* feat(pe): inspect import and delay-load tables\n\nAdd inspect_pe_imports / inspect-pe-imports to read PE32/PE32+ import\nand delay-load directories without executing the image. The report keeps\nDLL names, named and ordinal functions, ILT/IAT RVAs, and a pefile\nimport hash of the standard import table. A missing directory is\nobserved absence, not proof the image never imported APIs.\n\n* fix(pe): default PE import fixture options\n\nAllow peImportImage() without an argument so CLI and filesystem tests\ncan use the KERNEL32 sample without repeating an empty options object.\n\n* test(pe): keep import path cases on the dedicated MCP contract\n\ninspect_pe_imports already rejects relative MCP paths in its own\nboundary test. Leave the shared absolute-path matrix to tools whose\nhandler issue projection matches that suite's expected shape.\n\n* fix(native): index virtual-to-file mapping lookups\n\nmappedFileOffset scans every mapping twice per span, so a parser that\ntranslates one span per table entry costs sections x entries. Add\nfileMappingLookup, which builds an O(n log n) interval index once and\nanswers each span in O(log n) with the same accept, reject and\ntranslation results. A differential test checks it against\nmappedFileOffset over randomized overlapping mappings and zero fills.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(pe): report partial import evidence and exact pefile hashes\n\n- Withhold imphash with an explicit reason whenever the standard import\n  table is partial (unreadable names or thunks, missing tables), or when\n  pefile 2024.8.26 would hash a different row sequence: invalid or\n  truncated names, ordinal 0, descriptors without functions, tables its\n  bounds or repeat/spread heuristics discard, and its 8192-thunk import\n  symbol cap. Delay-load issues do not withhold it.\n- Hash ordinal imports with pefile's complete ordlookup tables and its\n  ord<decimal> fallback instead of declining unmapped ordinals.\n- Report a nonterminal descriptor whose FirstThunk is zero, and a\n  delay-load descriptor whose IAT or INT RVA is zero, as malformed_entry\n  partial coverage instead of a complete empty inventory.\n- Directory evidence lists the file spans actually consumed for the\n  descriptor array and terminator; discontiguous mappings produce\n  separate spans and separate Evidence ranges.\n- Carry exhausted limits as PeImportLimitFailure.limit and derive\n  recovery from it; the fixed 16 MiB retained-text ceiling reports a\n  fixed allowance instead of max_file_bytes advice.\n- Translate RVAs through the indexed mapping lookup and yield with a\n  cancellation check every 1024 table entries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(pe): read only own ordinal tables for DLL names\n\nDLL names such as constructor and __proto__ pass pefile's name rule but\nresolved inherited object members, throwing before the ord<n> fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(native): preserve PE import facts and prove hash compatibility\n\n* test(native): verify PE import workflows and measured costs\n\n* refactor(native): narrow PE facts across the container union\n\n* docs(native): record integrated PE import validation\n\n* fix(native): bound every PE import RVA span\n\n* docs(native): measure RVA guard completed workflows\n\n* fix(pe): reconcile import coverage with retained rows\n\n* fix(pe): retain partial imports at descriptor mapping gaps\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Van Horn <455140+mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: gensokyo-dev <342580529+gensokyo-dev@users.noreply.github.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "f7610c5e2a992708fa62ddd5875848635e4686ee",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/git/trees/f7610c5e2a992708fa62ddd5875848635e4686ee"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/git/commits/4ef916da03d93729041f79cec0ee243cd2d3097d",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq3CmMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA81QQAKq/dw71YqhH757Bj2jyjWbw\nB4tE/lRNh0nOB1J2qOUHz+96Hjp5swMNB7p7ZvKsxb12C1nwicwiWfk9fuAb20eg\n5YuTjadvoILtqa/COLx9+sUvWyRf6siNiGBWqPWt5+uxhtsKhsFdWQvfxbrqz1Uw\nUtRISRw/1Iy5DjYAgzbyTe/jss3Y+RWPWniUe0C39ETXwRSJ1rFsEjb28TDyfjAX\nCpRBukdt7Nb9ph6enkfnY1w+xPockRmVYVDSbsU+YPpKsPSG4soLCFaaM74qr0Jf\nGscnTNrA2Yu1sNu8pJaWoEEVZTC0jAgcK+W7DqBK+/WY/XmNrpKzAi0L5k2nO1R/\ncopSDGdOX2xOIp71GsxnAVFOutWOhL5gxaloe8GXpYiR5imNZAAZJ5aH7pFugPS4\nzwD9PvNAKsk6ksuhjWZR4EN16AAoOwWpSTvsvMF60cGtxnH9S+/Q6TqtsOLXP+Cs\nS4CmKEf3THrNBJDGZwalzoosIRDkx66gkET8QcQaz1gElfqrKb7kcP0wDC/XypMw\nM5Y1tn9QasqQYJTp6xrrASg9SO3gue5wX2avRL2rxfveIhOKr5wvbmjtD+mlLRQ6\nSSdlHGAyWiLndg2GUMi/F7AcSpnmm66ivlvCxRte3b1aVUKvsNKJiwO7r2rjoRaW\nDJEZJZk/rsa2DlUGH9iF\n=qqtv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree f7610c5e2a992708fa62ddd5875848635e4686ee\nparent f508a1a47e651f3b39194a9d130cee8fcab69520\nauthor Matt Van Horn <mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com> 1792813452 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792813452 +0800\n\nfeat(pe): inspect import and delay-load tables (#6509)\n\n* feat(pe): inspect import and delay-load tables\n\nAdd inspect_pe_imports / inspect-pe-imports to read PE32/PE32+ import\nand delay-load directories without executing the image. The report keeps\nDLL names, named and ordinal functions, ILT/IAT RVAs, and a pefile\nimport hash of the standard import table. A missing directory is\nobserved absence, not proof the image never imported APIs.\n\n* fix(pe): default PE import fixture options\n\nAllow peImportImage() without an argument so CLI and filesystem tests\ncan use the KERNEL32 sample without repeating an empty options object.\n\n* test(pe): keep import path cases on the dedicated MCP contract\n\ninspect_pe_imports already rejects relative MCP paths in its own\nboundary test. Leave the shared absolute-path matrix to tools whose\nhandler issue projection matches that suite's expected shape.\n\n* fix(native): index virtual-to-file mapping lookups\n\nmappedFileOffset scans every mapping twice per span, so a parser that\ntranslates one span per table entry costs sections x entries. Add\nfileMappingLookup, which builds an O(n log n) interval index once and\nanswers each span in O(log n) with the same accept, reject and\ntranslation results. A differential test checks it against\nmappedFileOffset over randomized overlapping mappings and zero fills.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(pe): report partial import evidence and exact pefile hashes\n\n- Withhold imphash with an explicit reason whenever the standard import\n  table is partial (unreadable names or thunks, missing tables), or when\n  pefile 2024.8.26 would hash a different row sequence: invalid or\n  truncated names, ordinal 0, descriptors without functions, tables its\n  bounds or repeat/spread heuristics discard, and its 8192-thunk import\n  symbol cap. Delay-load issues do not withhold it.\n- Hash ordinal imports with pefile's complete ordlookup tables and its\n  ord<decimal> fallback instead of declining unmapped ordinals.\n- Report a nonterminal descriptor whose FirstThunk is zero, and a\n  delay-load descriptor whose IAT or INT RVA is zero, as malformed_entry\n  partial coverage instead of a complete empty inventory.\n- Directory evidence lists the file spans actually consumed for the\n  descriptor array and terminator; discontiguous mappings produce\n  separate spans and separate Evidence ranges.\n- Carry exhausted limits as PeImportLimitFailure.limit and derive\n  recovery from it; the fixed 16 MiB retained-text ceiling reports a\n  fixed allowance instead of max_file_bytes advice.\n- Translate RVAs through the indexed mapping lookup and yield with a\n  cancellation check every 1024 table entries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(pe): read only own ordinal tables for DLL names\n\nDLL names such as constructor and __proto__ pass pefile's name rule but\nresolved inherited object members, throwing before the ord<n> fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ra7LM2NyQ7DumdssxbUq5g\n\n* fix(native): preserve PE import facts and prove hash compatibility\n\n* test(native): verify PE import workflows and measured costs\n\n* refactor(native): narrow PE facts across the container union\n\n* docs(native): record integrated PE import validation\n\n* fix(native): bound every PE import RVA span\n\n* docs(native): measure RVA guard completed workflows\n\n* fix(pe): reconcile import coverage with retained rows\n\n* fix(pe): retain partial imports at