  {
    "sha": "bfba99827e314b9f2469f46eb98c3e1f928abd7a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOSB6hVdoAKGJmYmE5OTgyN2UzMTRiOWYyNDY5ZjQ2ZWI5OGMzZTFmOTI4YWJkN2E",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Matt Van Horn",
        "email": "mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-22T09:46:15Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-22T09:46:15Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(erlang): inspect BEAM IFF chunks and tables (#4833)\n\n* feat(erlang): inspect BEAM IFF chunks and tables\n\nReplay the Erlang BEAM inspection workflow, including table bounds,\nOTP 28+ atom layouts, the shared absolute-path policy, and empty-path\nCLI coverage, without carrying GitHub workflow edits.\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(erlang): use publicInputStrictObject for BEAM tool input\n\ninspect_erlang_beam advertised a public input built with bare\nz.strictObject, so later shared input-policy changes would miss it.\nResult and internal objects stay on their own constructors.\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "52aca747f406ce521102e3e177f078a199e98ed8",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/git/trees/52aca747f406ce521102e3e177f078a199e98ed8"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/git/commits/bfba99827e314b9f2469f46eb98c3e1f928abd7a",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2dtnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAduoQABnp5hQnG9cn8iQk0xLY+9Lr\nl3GA7rJGKnb0AjyeMMa3kV9OzaHYLZwweP/2jxzU7AR/lRgxpVOjyQl6skZqmzYb\ntw9I8K0jEX7lAicqaNl7dkHrgIRo024Tj7RwXEQiulwNBFTCVtPRvmZq9TuA3yI8\nK3OxirmVusXsQZWXPSsNcnC5SD5SohwHnn420SK0qJp1VpoFdoYfwLEDne/9EyXO\njV1I4M1VlYmKwvJS8mdywR2Mvv3YLYP9XU62frpd9G47Nl+1xMENkU0ZEvOEndq5\nERRguH7qDPX5w4RW6ZAPxKcLmyTZWW3ZfcxVdmMT+5+Hea7bKS4+D/m/rZ5INotz\nJaxdIanjLsf5EW+xXaCuXwxZl5OY7JVcUWN/e+ZiFV7W70+BIC9rChEVQ66qdyq3\nKIlM24bPe/Ax8wLqpuOu6cLXcUbnvyficFEThynmsrjVDm3JGEauTPBQlQWFPPsr\nwAmVP2Z/vLdc7L1Y2yu2q3JPg5YG7OXhDE8wiAvSNjqxDriGY9sMPAArdmCaBLhi\nCvrvI1avmxKOjr28wNpgrhcDjEfwtmssjg9Nr1BXMnGuWoiRLyhKyswWNMGCT5Rj\ng7GN0jVu3U+harh0oWImCMk56NMsGkvxpmfCOQqkFANqwtDthL7lPhM0JkkNC7rX\n9DjvOg5QzJW0K+ftryfL\n=GS4D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 52aca747f406ce521102e3e177f078a199e98ed8\nparent 44827a502004997738296f040dde04d9ed942bed\nauthor Matt Van Horn <mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com> 1792662375 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792662375 +0800\n\nfeat(erlang): inspect BEAM IFF chunks and tables (#4833)\n\n* feat(erlang): inspect BEAM IFF chunks and tables\n\nReplay the Erlang BEAM inspection workflow, including table bounds,\nOTP 28+ atom layouts, the shared absolute-path policy, and empty-path\nCLI coverage, without carrying GitHub workflow edits.\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(erlang): use publicInputStrictObject for BEAM tool input\n\ninspect_erlang_beam advertised a public input built with bare\nz.strictObject, so later shared input-policy changes would miss it.\nResult and internal objects stay on their own constructors.\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
